note Exercism-style exercise "resistor-color-trio": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/resistor-color-trio
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note colors holds band color names joined by commas (black 0, brown 1, red 2, orange 3, yellow 4,
note green 5, blue 6, violet 7, grey 8, white 9). The first two bands give a two-digit number, the
note third the count of zeros after it; further bands are ignored. label writes the resistance as
note "<number> <unit>" into o, with the largest of ohms, kiloohms, megaohms, gigaohms that keeps the
note number whole, and returns the number of bytes written.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/resistor-color-trio
om2
fn label colors view uchar * o edit uchar * to ulong
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
